---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'November 2026';

const webPageSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Refund & Cancellation Policy | ListLift',
  url: 'https://listlift.com/refunds',
  dateModified: '2026-11-22',
  description:
    'ListLift Refund & Cancellation Policy: 1-click subscription cancellation anytime, 7-day first-time subscriber refund window, and clear processing timeline.',
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Refund & Cancellation Policy"
  description="ListLift Refund & Cancellation Policy: 1-click subscription cancellation anytime, 7-day first-time subscriber refund window, and fast support timeline."
  canonicalPath="/refunds"
  jsonLd={webPageSchema}
>
  <article class="container legal-shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="legal-header">
      <span class="badge badge-pass">Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</span>
      <h1>Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted legal-intro">
        We want trying ListLift to be risk-free. You can test our Listing Studio and free tools before subscribing, and paid subscriptions follow the clear cancellation and refund rules below.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="card legal-body">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Subscription Cancellation (Cancel Anytime)</h2>
        <p>
          You can cancel your Pro or Business subscription at any time with one click from your account dashboard or billing portal before your next billing date.
        </p>
        <p>
          After canceling, you will not be charged again, and your paid access continues until the end of your current paid billing period.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. 7-Day Refund Eligibility Window</h2>
        <p>
          We offer a <strong>7-day refund window</strong> for first-time paid subscribers if ListLift experiences a technical defect or does not work as described on our website, subject to fair-use limits:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The refund request is submitted within <strong>7 calendar days</strong> of your initial subscription payment.</li>
          <li>Your account has used <strong>fewer than 15 listing generations</strong> during that billing period (to prevent bulk catalog extraction followed by refund abuse).</li>
          <li>If our support team cannot resolve a verified technical issue affecting your workflow, we will issue a full refund to your original payment method.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Non-Refundable Cases</h2>
        <p>To keep pricing affordable for all sellers, refunds are not available in the following situations:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Partial months or unused time requested after the 7-day initial window has passed.</li>
          <li>Subscription renewal charges that were not canceled prior to the renewal date (you can cancel anytime before renewal to stop future charges).</li>
          <li>Accounts that have exceeded the 15-generation fair-use threshold or exported bulk catalogs.</li>
          <li>Accounts suspended or terminated for violating our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> (such as bot abuse or prohibited goods).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. How to Request a Refund</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Email <a href="mailto:[support@yourdomain.com]">[support@yourdomain.com]</a> (or use our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>) with the subject line <code>Refund Request</code>.</li>
          <li>Include the email address used at checkout, your order/invoice ID, and a brief note on what went wrong.</li>
          <li><strong>Response time:</strong> Our team reviews and replies within <strong>24 to 48 business hours</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Processing time:</strong> Approved refunds are issued immediately through our payment processor (Paddle, Lemon Squeezy, Stripe, or Razorpay) and typically appear on your statement within <strong>5 to 10 business days</strong> depending on your bank.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Billing Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Operated by <strong>[Your Company Legal Name, City, Country]</strong>.<br />
          Billing Support: <a href="mailto:[support@yourdomain.com]">[support@yourdomain.com]</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-shell {
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .legal-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .legal-header h1 {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .legal-intro {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .legal-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 34px);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .legal-body h2 {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-size: 1.22rem;
  }
  .legal-body p {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .legal-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .legal-body ul,
  .legal-body ol {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .legal-body strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
